@* Styles of the expenses, reconciliation and accounting screens (rendered once by each page; the back office has no CSS
   isolation bundle). Text keeps a contrast of at least 4.5:1; a status is shown by its text, never by its colour alone.
   Logical properties for the future right-to-left layout. *@
<style>
    .accounting-facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 2rem; margin: 0; }
    .accounting-facts dt { color: #4a5361; font-size: 0.8125rem; }
    .accounting-facts dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 500; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .accounting-number { text-align: end; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .accounting-muted { color: #4a5361; }
    .accounting-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
    .accounting-scroll .mud-table-container { overflow: visible; }
    .accounting-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #0b57d0; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .accounting-total td { font-weight: 700; border-block-start: 1px solid #1b1f24; }
    .accounting-deleted td { text-decoration: line-through; color: #4a5361; }
    .accounting-deleted td.accounting-keep { text-decoration: none; }
</style>
